## 44. MUNICIPALITIES

**[SYL: GS2-F.2] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 44] | [74TH AMENDMENT ACT, 1992]**

### 44.1. Introduction

74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992 gave constitutional status to urban local bodies. Came into force on **1 June 1993**. Added **Part IX-A** and **Twelfth Schedule** (18 subjects).

### 44.2. Types of Municipalities (Art. 243Q)

- **Nagar Panchayat:** For transitional areas (rural to urban)
- **Municipal Council:** For smaller urban areas
- **Municipal Corporation:** For larger urban areas

### 44.3. Salient Features
- **Constitution:** Three types as per Article 243Q
- **Election:** Direct elections to all seats (Art. 243R)
- **Reservation:** SC/ST as per population, 1/3 for women (Art. 243T)
- **Duration:** 5 years (Art. 243U)
- **State Election Commission:** Conducts elections (Art. 243ZA)
- **State Finance Commission:** Reviews finances (Art. 243YE)
- **Powers:** For 18 subjects in Twelfth Schedule (Art. 243W)

### 44.4. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | 74th Amendment added which Part? | 74th Amendment | Part IX-A |
| 2017 | Prelims | Twelfth Schedule has how many subjects? | Schedule | 18 subjects |
| 2018 | Mains | Urban local governance and 74th Amendment | Municipalities | Decentralization, planning, finances |

### 44.5. MIND MAP

```text
MUNICIPALITIES - 74TH AMENDMENT 1992
├── ADDED: Part IX-A, Twelfth Schedule (18 subjects)
├── TYPES: Nagar Panchayat, Municipal Council, Municipal Corporation
├── RESERVATION: SC/ST + 1/3 women
├── SEC, SFC, 5 YEAR TERM
└── URBAN LOCAL SELF-GOVERNMENT
```

